Test-only. Three mutants on #2916 merge resolutions survived every test reaching the mutated code
(sweep t_01a1d9691f433636, main a3fe7bf2c7):

- M2c gateway/run_runtime.py::recover_profile_native_sessions: `_prime_recovered_egress(bindings)`
  moved into `asyncio.to_thread`. New test_native_recovery_primes_adapter_routing_cache_on_the_loop
  records threading.get_ident() in a fake adapter's prime_routing_cache and asserts it runs on the loop
  thread, before recover_native_sessions.
- M4b agent/auxiliary_client.py::_recover_provider_pool passing "" for base_url, and
- M4c _recover_failure_pool dropping base_url= : new
  test_aux_429_on_a_base_url_override_rotates_the_row_bound_to_that_address drives a real aux 429
  through call_llm against a custom entry with rows on two base_urls; it asserts the NEW-origin row
  that sent the request is marked exhausted and the call rotates to its NEW sibling, never the
  OLD-origin row.

Proof (sdlc-review mutants.py, specs = the sweep's run2 files with root/HOME updated):
  item2 baseline 10 files, 95 passed, 0 failed; M2c killed by the new boot-recovery test.
  item4 baseline 7 files, 228 passed, 0 failed; M4b and M4c each killed by both parametrizations.
Production diff: empty.

